# Normalize line endings to LF in the repo AND in the working tree on every
# platform. Without this, Git for Windows (autocrlf=true, the GitHub Actions
# windows-latest default) checks these files out with CRLF, and Vite's
# shebang handling then fails to parse the `.mjs` check scripts with
# "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" — which took down the entire
# Vitest step on windows-latest in the first CI run of S1.
#
# `eol=lf` is deliberate (rather than plain `text`): these files are executed
# by Node and parsed by Vite on both platforms, so they must be byte-identical
# everywhere, not normalized-on-commit-and-converted-on-checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.dmg binary
*.msi binary
*.exe binary
